## LEAN profile (VARIANT=minimal + LEAN=true): the headless essentials
## only — no kali-linux-core baseline, no git/tmux/tcpdump/dislocker.
## The stick still boots headless, joins Wi-Fi, takes SSH keys, runs the
## mesh (wg + fips daemon) and the rescue channel. Everything not needed
## to reach sshd over wifi/wg is out.
openssh-server
network-manager
wpasupplicant
wireless-regdb
## Radio firmware, EXPLICIT (2026-10-28, owner direction: no firmware diet —
## inclusion by default). These arrived only transitively via upstream's
## pinned lists before, so an upstream list change could silently strip them
## (the #51 Legion incident: iwlwifi failed with error -1010 + hci0 could not
## read supported features — root cause there was a Windows-fast-startup
## wedged combo card, but the image must never be the variable).
## iwlwifi covers ALL Intel wireless generations (212 ucode files in #44);
## ibt-* Intel Bluetooth blobs ship in firmware-iwlwifi's intel tree.
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-linux-nonfree
firmware-misc-nonfree
firmware-atheros
firmware-brcm80211
firmware-realtek
bluez-firmware

iw
iproute2
avahi-daemon
## mDNS client NSS module: <name>.local resolution is how the boot-time
## duplicate-hostname probe sees other machines (avahi-daemon only recommends it)
libnss-mdns
curl
python3
openssl
ca-certificates
sudo
e2fsprogs
## FAT32 for the KLHCONFIG partition (auto-create + flash reuse; found
## missing from minimal on hardware 2026-10-25: partition appended, no fs)
dosfstools
## WireGuard access channel (identical to the standard profile)
wireguard-tools
## BitLocker unlock for the NTFS vm store (rides the KVM stack)
dislocker
systemd-timesyncd
